      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Module 04 — Verification Portal: Status\nStreamlit UI (`ui-engine`, port 8501) · 573-line `app.py` · Snapshot: 2026-07-30, `main-demo` @ `5c65046` (FINAL)",
      "x": 230,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 110,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "working-http",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Working: all three engine pages over HTTP**\nSpec (`POST spec-engine:8000/verify`), Extract (`POST extract-engine:8000/verify`), Equiv (`POST equiv-engine:8000/lift`). Sidebar dots are real health checks for all three engines (`GET /docs` ×2, `GET /health`, 2s timeout) — the old asymmetry is gone",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -80,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 190,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "equiv-fixed",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**FIXED: Equiv page (PR #74)**\nWas broken by construction (in-process `import vibecheck_lifter` in a container with no SPOT). Root cause was upstream: M03 had no HTTP service. M03's `main.py` rewritten as FastAPI (`/lift`, `/check`, `/health`); the page now calls `/lift` over HTTP like the other pages",
      "x": 520,
      "y": -80,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 190,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "networkx",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**FIXED: unused `networkx` removed (PR #84)**\nConfirmed zero references first; `ui-engine` rebuilt and serving 200 without it",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 160,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "naming-fixed",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Fixed earlier: naming collision**\nUI no longer confuses V1/V2/V3 verification layers with module numbers; certificate figures are live results parsed from engine HTTP responses",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 160,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-gap",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Gap: `POST /check` has no UI demo**\nFull Phase A–D conformance needs a call-order-lifted WIR; extract-engine's `/verify` now returns `call_order_wir`, but the UI doesn't yet chain the two calls — the page documents this itself",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 170,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "zero-tests",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Gap: zero tests**\nNo test suite exists for Module 04 (one `app.py`, a 12-line Dockerfile, 2-line requirements)",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify-caveat",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Caveat: PR #74 verification was local-only**\nEquiv service verified against a scratchpad-built `.so`; the docker-compose SPOT build and the Streamlit page in a real browser were not verified in that session — flagged, not claimed",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 540,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "scope",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Scope disclaimer**\nStill explicitly disclaims research novelty: a UI/integration layer, not a research contribution — hence no novelty document for this module",
      "x": 520,
